            {
              "claim": "Mauro Chehab (media maintainer): the kernel's Coverity instance sees only code that builds on x86, and his own per-patch builds are i386 only, so non-x86 code is a blind spot for both static analysis and per-patch builds. 2017, foundational.",
              "quote": "the Coverity instance we use on Kernel works only for the code that builds on x86.",
              "url": "https://lkml.iu.edu/hypermail/linux/kernel/1706.0/05161.html",
