            {
              "claim": "Gazzillo/Yildiran OSS NA 2022 slides (read as images): v5.13, 13,411 commits; defconfig fully covers 1,688 and one randconfig 2,189; 8,853 and 8,333 not covered; 1,296 non-x86 and 1,177 header-only excluded. Slide 9 states the problem: no guarantee a committed change is built. Slide 8: allyesconfig does not include all code because of mutually exclusive options and multiple architectures. Line/commit-level, not object-level.",
              "quote": "no guarantee that committed changes get built",
              "url": "https://paulgazzillo.com/files/oss2022.pdf",
