              "reopened_and_verified": true
            },
            {
              "claim": "krepair paper (FSE 2024) Section 2 motivating case: a leak persisted for months because the controlling option was not enabled in the tested configs. Same paper: 36,115 Intel 0-day reports with configs (Oct 2019 to Aug 2022) were 63% randconfig, 15% allyesconfig, 7% defconfig, 7% allmodconfig; mutual exclusion prevents allyesconfig from covering all code.",
              "quote": "remained in the kernel for months, because the configuration option controlling inclusion of the buggy code was not enabled",
