            {
              "claim": "LWN report of the 2025 Maintainers Summit linux-next session (Corbet's wording, indirect speech, not a Torvalds quote): allmodconfig builds disable some code and can hide problems, and Ojeda did not want people testing with canned configurations. Supports the blindspot half of D6(a) and also shows that a canonical minimal set is contested.",
              "quote": "cause some code to be disabled, and can thus hide problems",
              "url": "https://lwn.net/Articles/1050027/",
