              "claim": "LWN report of the 2022 Maintainers Summit (Corbet's wording): Brown said comprehensive tests are hard to turn around within the 24 hours a linux-next release exists, and Torvalds said KernelCI testing does not really cover drivers. The 24-hour window is the time budget that D6(b) skipping would relax. The article does not discuss build configs.",
