            {
              "claim": "CIP maintains per-config 'potentially used source' lists (.sources) for its boards. They are produced by a full kernel build with a compiler wrapper (scripts/get_used_sources.py runs mrproper, oldconfig, then make) and added to git. This is the object-set-per-config question answered by building. The lists also add all non-C/H/S files from git conservatively.",
              "quote": "requires running a complete kernel build process",
              "url": "https://gitlab.com/cip-project/cip-kernel/cip-kernel-config/-/raw/master/README.md",
              "date": "current repo (n.d.)",
              "evidence_type": "tool",
              "source_group": "CIP cip-kernel-config",
              "reopened_and_verified": true
            },
            {
              "claim": "OpenWrt: each kmod package hand-lists its .ko paths in FILES, and the install step fails when a listed module was not produced. It prints a NOTICE instead when the module is built in. Checks happen at package time, after the kernel build.",
              "quote": "echo \"ERROR: module '$$$$$$$$mod' is missing.\" >&2;",
              "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/openwrt/openwrt/main/include/kernel.mk",
              "date": "main as of 2026-10-17",
              "evidence_type": "tool",
              "source_group": "OpenWrt kernel.mk",
              "reopened_and_verified": true
            },
            {
              "claim": "OpenWrt-devel 2015: the build config set AES to =y but crypto.mk still defined kmod-crypto-aes, which ships an autoload entry for a .ko the build never produces. The build did not fail. The reporter asked whether the package or the =y setting was wrong. This is a config-versus-object mismatch found by a human; old.",
              "quote": "trying to load a module which doesn't exist.",
              "url": "https://lists.openwrt.org/pipermail/openwrt-devel/2015-July/008154.html",
              "date": "2015-07-08",
              "evidence_type": "anecdote",
              "source_group": "OpenWrt-devel 2015",
              "reopened_and_verified": true
            },
            {
              "claim": "OpenWrt forum, 2020-04-25: a user added a KernelPackage for DVB modules; CONFIG_MEDIA_TUNER_SI2157 was in .config.old but missing from the kernel .config, so the .ko files were never built. No confirmed fix in six replies; one 2023 poster blamed new compiler warnings. The cause is mixed: part Kconfig, part code.",
              "quote": "ERROR: module '/media/brouwer/.../drivers/media/tuners/si2157.ko' is missing.",
              "url": "https://forum.openwrt.org/t/ko-file-not-being-compiled-after-adding-kernel-package/61768",
              "date": "2020-04-25",
              "evidence_type": "anecdote",
