            },
            {
              "claim": "PatchLens states its own limit on headers, which also bounds a file-level approach: header fixes are under-reported because the transitive effect on including translation units is not modelled.",
              "quote": "PatchLens does not model the transitive effect of changes in header files",
              "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2606.25863",
              "evidence_type": "tool",
              "source_group": "PatchLens (Paixao et al.)",
              "date": "2026-07",
              "reopened_and_verified": true
            },
            {
              "claim": "cvehound maps a CVE to config from Kbuild/Makefiles only and does not check #ifdefs. It accepts a .config via --kernel-config; files it cannot map are reported 'unknown' and counted as affected; --check-strict drops a CVE only if every file is ruled out. No accuracy numbers. The repo's issue tracker shows one open issue, from 2021, unrelated to config.",
              "quote": "ifdefs are not checked",
