              "reopened_and_verified": true
            },
            {
              "claim": "barebox CI patch: sandbox allyesconfig is built and tested so that treewide changes do not break compile-only drivers that normal defconfigs never build. Shows a second bootloader project paying for a whole-config build to approximate 'every object compiles somewhere'.",
              "quote": "allows us to catch early compile-time breakage when changes are done treewide.",
              "url": "https://www.mail-archive.com/barebox@lists.infradead.org/msg52399.html",
              "date": "2025-03-26",
              "evidence_type": "policy",
              "source_group": "barebox list 2025 allyesconfig CI (Fatoum)",
              "reopened_and_verified": true
            },
            {
              "claim": "Report of the 2025 Maintainers Summit linux-next session (the article's wording, not a transcript): allmodconfig builds disable some code and so can hide problems. Direct maintainer-level testimony that one standard config does not build everything. The same report has Ojeda against canned configurations.",
              "quote": "cause some code to be disabled, and can thus hide problems",
              "url": "https://lwn.net/Articles/1050027/",
              "date": "2025-12-12",
              "evidence_type": "anecdote",
